XWayland: retain tiled placement intent for fullscreen output selection

Wine can request a different monitor before entering fullscreen. Keep the
requested destination while rejecting geometry changes to normal tiles,
then consume it for the client fullscreen transition. Also honor monitor
changes requested after fullscreen, using compositor output geometry.
Resize-only requests, offscreen targets, and ignoreConfigureRequest rules
do not override placement. Do not change Proton rendering or scaling.

--- a/include/xwayland.h
+++ b/include/xwayland.h
@@ -40,6 +40,13 @@
 	struct wlr_xwayland_surface *xwayland_surface;
 	bool focused_before_map;
 	bool initial_geometry_set;
+
+	/* Last tiled client placement request, consumed when entering fullscreen.
+	 * Store coordinates rather than an output pointer to survive hot-unplug.
+	 * A changed source output invalidates the request (e.g. a user move).
+	 */
+	struct wlr_box fullscreen_request_geometry;
+	uint64_t fullscreen_request_from_output;
 
 	/* Events unique to XWayland views */
 	struct wl_listener associate;
